  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_HUMANHEALTHANDDISEASE_DIAGRAM_Q01 - Structure of an antibody molecule</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>The given diagram represents the structure of an antibody molecule (\(\mathrm{H_2L_2}\)). Identify the parts labelled <strong>X</strong>, <strong>Y</strong>, and <strong>Z</strong> correctly.</p>
      <p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 420 280" width="420" height="280" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #d9d9d9;">
          <!-- Heavy chains (Y-shaped) -->
          <polygon points="185,250 200,250 200,145 140,70 128,80 185,150" fill="#e67e22" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="235,250 220,250 220,145 280,70 292,80 235,150" fill="#e67e22" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <!-- Variable regions on heavy chains -->
          <polygon points="140,70 128,80 105,52 117,42" fill="#3498db" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="280,70 292,80 315,52 303,42" fill="#3498db" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <!-- Light chains -->
          <polygon points="148,150 160,140 125,98 113,108" fill="#e74c3c" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="272,150 260,140 295,98 307,108" fill="#e74c3c" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <!-- Variable regions on light chains -->
          <polygon points="125,98 113,108 88,78 100,68" fill="#f1c40f" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="295,98 307,108 332,78 320,68" fill="#f1c40f" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <!-- Disulfide bonds -->
          <line x1="200" y1="165" x2="220" y2="165" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="210" y="162" font-size="9" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">S-S</text>
          <line x1="200" y1="185" x2="220" y2="185" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="210" y="182" font-size="9" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">S-S</text>
          <line x1="160" y1="140" x2="176" y2="138" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <line x1="260" y1="140" x2="244" y2="138" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <!-- N and C termini -->
          <text x="102" y="38" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">N</text>
          <text x="312" y="38" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">N</text>
          <text x="192" y="266" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">C</text>
          <text x="225" y="266" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">C</text>
          <!-- Label X: Antigen binding site -->
          <line x1="95" y1="55" x2="65" y2="35" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="52" y="38" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#000" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">X</text>
          <!-- Label Y: Light chain -->
          <line x1="130" y1="130" x2="75" y2="145" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="58" y="150" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#000" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Y</text>
          <!-- Label Z: Heavy chain -->
          <line x1="185" y1="215" x2="115" y2="215" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="98" y="220" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#000" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Z</text>
        </svg>
      </p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Given Data and Conditions</strong><br/>The diagram shows a Y-shaped antibody molecule composed of four polypeptide chains linked by disulfide (\(\mathrm{-S-S-}\)) bonds. Label <strong>X</strong> points to the cleft at the N-terminal tip between the upper arms, label <strong>Y</strong> points to one of the two shorter outer polypeptide chains, and label <strong>Z</strong> points to one of the two longer central polypeptide chains extending down to the C-terminal stem.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Assumptions and Sign Conventions</strong><br/>The schematic follows the standard structural representation of an immunoglobulin monomer (\(\mathrm{H_2L_2}\)) as presented in NCERT Class 12 Biology, with the N-termini at the upper antigen-recognising ends and the C-termini at the lower stem.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Relevant Formulae and Principles</strong><br/>Each antibody molecule consists of four peptide chains: two small chains called light chains (\(\mathrm{L}\)) and two longer chains called heavy chains (\(\mathrm{H}\)), represented as \(\mathrm{H_2L_2}\). The variable regions of one heavy chain and one light chain at each N-terminal tip together form an antigen-binding site.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>1. <strong>X</strong> indicates the pocket formed by the N-terminal variable regions of the heavy and light chains, which is the <strong>antigen binding site</strong>.<br/>2. <strong>Y</strong> indicates the shorter outer polypeptide chain, which is the <strong>light chain</strong>.<br/>3. <strong>Z</strong> indicates the longer inner polypeptide chain forming the stem and arms, which is the <strong>heavy chain</strong>.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 5: Check and Final Answer</strong><br/>Matching the structure against \(\mathrm{H_2L_2}\) confirms two heavy chains, two light chains, and two antigen-binding sites at the N-termini. Therefore, <strong>X</strong> is the antigen binding site, <strong>Y</strong> is the light chain, and <strong>Z</strong> is the heavy chain.</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>X – Heavy chain, Y – Antigen binding site, Z – Light chain</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>X – Antigen binding site, Y – Light chain, Z – Heavy chain</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>X – Constant region, Y – Heavy chain, Z – Disulfide bond</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>X – Antigen binding site, Y – Heavy chain, Z – Light chain</p>]]></text></answer>
