  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_HUMANHEALTHANDDISEASE_DIAGRAM_Q02 - Life cycle stages of Plasmodium</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>The schematic below illustrates the life cycle of <em>Plasmodium</em> across its two hosts. Identify <strong>P</strong>, <strong>Q</strong>, <strong>R</strong>, and <strong>S</strong> correctly.</p>
      <p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 520 300" width="520" height="300" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #d9d9d9;">
          <!-- Dividing line between Mosquito Host and Human Host -->
          <line x1="250" y1="20" x2="250" y2="280" stroke="#888" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="6,4"/>
          <text x="125" y="30" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#2c3e50" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Mosquito Host</text>
          <text x="385" y="30" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c0392b" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Human Host</text>
          <!-- Top: Mosquito bite injects P -->
          <rect x="175" y="45" width="170" height="36" rx="6" fill="#fef5e7" stroke="#d35400" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="260" y="67" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Mosquito bite injects <tspan font-weight="bold">P</tspan></text>
          <!-- Arrow to Q -->
          <line x1="345" y1="63" x2="405" y2="95" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="405,95 395,94 401,86" fill="#333"/>
          <!-- Box Q -->
          <rect x="330" y="95" width="160" height="40" rx="6" fill="#fadbd8" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="410" y="113" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Asexual multiplication</text>
          <text x="410" y="128" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">inside <tspan font-weight="bold">Q</tspan></text>
          <!-- Arrow to R -->
          <line x1="410" y1="135" x2="410" y2="175" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="410,175 406,166 414,166" fill="#333"/>
          <!-- Box R -->
          <rect x="320" y="175" width="180" height="44" rx="6" fill="#fadbd8" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="410" y="194" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Parasites burst <tspan font-weight="bold">R</tspan>, releasing</text>
          <text x="410" y="209" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">haemozoin &amp; gametocytes</text>
          <!-- Arrow to Mosquito uptake -->
          <line x1="320" y1="245" x2="220" y2="245" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="220,245 229,241 229,249" fill="#333"/>
          <line x1="410" y1="219" x2="410" y2="245" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <line x1="410" y1="245" x2="320" y2="245" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <!-- Mosquito uptake box -->
          <rect x="35" y="225" width="185" height="40" rx="6" fill="#ebf5fb" stroke="#2980b9" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="127" y="243" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Female <tspan font-style="italic">Anopheles</tspan> takes up</text>
          <text x="127" y="258" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">gametocytes with blood meal</text>
          <!-- Arrow to S -->
          <line x1="127" y1="225" x2="127" y2="180" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="127,180 123,189 131,189" fill="#333"/>
          <!-- Box S -->
          <rect x="35" y="135" width="185" height="45" rx="6" fill="#ebf5fb" stroke="#2980b9" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="127" y="155" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Fertilisation and development</text>
          <text x="127" y="170" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">occur in <tspan font-weight="bold">S</tspan></text>
          <!-- Arrow to Salivary glands & back to P -->
          <line x1="127" y1="135" x2="127" y2="75" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <line x1="127" y1="75" x2="175" y2="63" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="175,63 165,61 168,69" fill="#333"/>
          <text x="115" y="108" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="end" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Migrate to</text>
          <text x="115" y="120" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="end" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">salivary glands</text>
        </svg>
      </p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Given Data and Conditions</strong><br/>The diagram traces the digenetic life cycle of <em>Plasmodium</em> between the mosquito host and the human host. Label <strong>P</strong> is the infectious stage injected during a mosquito bite, <strong>Q</strong> is the first human organ where asexual multiplication occurs, <strong>R</strong> represents the blood cells ruptured to release haemozoin and form gametocytes, and <strong>S</strong> is the site of fertilisation and development inside the mosquito.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Assumptions and Sign Conventions</strong><br/>Arrows indicate the sequential direction of transmission and developmental stages in the two-host cycle of the malarial parasite.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Relevant Formulae and Principles</strong><br/><em>Plasmodium</em> requires two hosts (human and female <em>Anopheles</em> mosquito) to complete its life cycle. In humans, asexual reproduction occurs first in hepatocytes and then in erythrocytes. In the mosquito, sexual fusion (fertilisation) and further development occur before mature infective stages migrate to the salivary glands.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>1. When an infected female <em>Anopheles</em> mosquito bites a human, it injects the infectious form called <strong>sporozoites</strong> (<strong>P</strong>).<br/>2. Sporozoites reach the <strong>liver</strong> (<strong>Q</strong>) through the blood and reproduce asexually in liver cells.<br/>3. Parasites then attack and reproduce asexually in <strong>red blood cells</strong> (<strong>R</strong>), bursting them to release haemozoin and forming sexual stages (gametocytes).<br/>4. When a female mosquito takes up gametocytes with a blood meal, fertilisation and development take place in the <strong>mosquito's gut</strong> (<strong>S</strong>), after which sporozoites migrate to the salivary glands.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 5: Check and Final Answer</strong><br/>Each stage aligns sequentially with the two-host cycle. Thus, <strong>P</strong> is sporozoites, <strong>Q</strong> is liver, <strong>R</strong> is red blood cells, and <strong>S</strong> is mosquito's gut.</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P – Gametocytes, Q – Spleen, R – White blood cells, S – Salivary glands</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P – Sporozoites, Q – Red blood cells, R – Liver cells, S – Mosquito's gut</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P – Merozoites, Q – Liver, R – Red blood cells, S – Proboscis</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P – Sporozoites, Q – Liver, R – Red blood cells, S – Mosquito's gut</p>]]></text></answer>
