  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_HUMANHEALTHANDDISEASE_DIAGRAM_Q03 - Replication of retrovirus inside animal cell</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>Study the given schematic representation of the replication of a retrovirus (such as HIV) inside an animal cell. Identify process <strong>P</strong>, enzyme <strong>Q</strong>, and product <strong>R</strong> correctly.</p>
      <p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 480 290" width="480" height="290" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #d9d9d9;">
          <!-- Retrovirus outside -->
          <circle cx="70" cy="50" r="22" fill="#f5eef8" stroke="#8e44ad" stroke-width="2"/>
          <path d="M58,48 Q65,38 72,48 T84,48" fill="none" stroke="#8e44ad" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="70" y="18" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Retrovirus (RNA)</text>
          <!-- Animal cell boundary -->
          <rect x="120" y="55" width="335" height="190" rx="12" fill="#eafaf1" stroke="#27ae60" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="445" y="72" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="end" fill="#1e8449" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Animal Cell (Cytoplasm)</text>
          <!-- Entry arrow -->
          <line x1="92" y1="50" x2="145" y2="85" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="145,85 135,84 141,76" fill="#333"/>
          <!-- Viral RNA inside -->
          <rect x="145" y="75" width="105" height="28" rx="4" fill="#fff" stroke="#8e44ad" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <text x="197" y="93" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Viral RNA</text>
          <!-- Process P and Enzyme Q -->
          <line x1="197" y1="103" x2="197" y2="140" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="197,140 193,131 201,131" fill="#333"/>
          <text x="205" y="120" font-size="11" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Process <tspan font-weight="bold">P</tspan></text>
          <text x="205" y="133" font-size="11" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">by enzyme <tspan font-weight="bold">Q</tspan></text>
          <!-- Viral DNA -->
          <rect x="145" y="140" width="105" height="28" rx="4" fill="#fff" stroke="#2980b9" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <text x="197" y="158" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Viral DNA</text>
          <!-- Arrow to Nucleus -->
          <line x1="250" y1="154" x2="320" y2="154" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="320,154 311,150 311,158" fill="#333"/>
          <!-- Nucleus -->
          <circle cx="375" cy="154" r="52" fill="#fef9e7" stroke="#b7950b" stroke-width="1.8"/>
          <text x="375" y="128" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Nucleus</text>
          <text x="375" y="146" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Viral DNA</text>
          <text x="375" y="160" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">incorporates into</text>
          <text x="375" y="174" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">host genome</text>
          <!-- Arrow from Nucleus to R -->
          <line x1="340" y1="194" x2="295" y2="205" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="295,205 305,207 302,199" fill="#333"/>
          <!-- Box R -->
          <rect x="155" y="195" width="140" height="32" rx="4" fill="#fff" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <text x="225" y="215" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">Product <tspan font-weight="bold">R</tspan> produced</text>
          <!-- Arrow to new viruses outside -->
          <line x1="155" y1="211" x2="90" y2="245" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="90,245 100,244 96,237" fill="#333"/>
          <circle cx="65" cy="255" r="18" fill="#f5eef8" stroke="#8e44ad" stroke-width="1.8"/>
          <text x="155" y="268" font-size="11" text-anchor="start" font-family="Arial, sans-serif">New viruses infect other cells</text>
        </svg>
      </p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Given Data and Conditions</strong><br/>The schematic depicts a retrovirus (such as HIV) infecting a normal animal cell (such as a macrophage). Viral RNA is introduced into the cytoplasm and converted by process <strong>P</strong> using enzyme <strong>Q</strong> into viral DNA, which integrates into the host genome in the nucleus to direct synthesis of product <strong>R</strong> for assembling progeny viruses.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Assumptions and Sign Conventions</strong><br/>The pathway follows the retroviral replication cycle described in NCERT Class 12 Biology, where the infected host cell survives while viruses are replicated and released.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Relevant Formulae and Principles</strong><br/>Retroviruses possess an RNA genome and synthesise a complementary viral DNA copy inside the host cell via RNA-dependent DNA synthesis. The integrated viral DNA (provirus) is then transcribed by the host cell's machinery to produce new viral RNA genomes and viral proteins.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>1. Conversion of viral RNA into viral DNA is called <strong>reverse transcription</strong> (<strong>P</strong>).<br/>2. This step is catalysed by the viral enzyme <strong>reverse transcriptase</strong> (<strong>Q</strong>).<br/>3. Once the viral DNA incorporates into the host cell's DNA, it directs the infected cell to produce <strong>new viral RNA</strong> (<strong>R</strong>) to assemble progeny viruses.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 5: Check and Final Answer</strong><br/>Checking the flow from RNA to DNA and back to viral RNA confirms retroviral replication. Thus, <strong>P</strong> is reverse transcription, <strong>Q</strong> is reverse transcriptase, and <strong>R</strong> is new viral RNA.</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P – Reverse transcription, Q – Reverse transcriptase, R – New viral RNA</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P – Transcription, Q – RNA polymerase, R – Viral DNA</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P – Translation, Q – DNA ligase, R – Capsid proteins only</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P – Replication, Q – DNA polymerase, R – Host mRNA</p>]]></text></answer>
